WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 3: Life in the Wild.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:09.580
In this unit, you will explore the natural world
through the lens of East African ecosystems.

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.040
You will discover how animals, plants, and
their environments are connected in amazing ways.

4
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.740
Every living thing depends on something else to survive,

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.820
and understanding these connections helps
us take better care of the world around us.

6
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:29.880
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:35.820
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
describe how food chains and ecosystems work,

8
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.400
using the correct scientific vocabulary.

9
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.920
You will also use the present simple tense
to state facts about animals and nature.

10
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:50.360
You will also build complex sentences using
relative clauses with who, which, and where.

11
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.880
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:00:53.460 --> 00:01:01.280
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: curiosity,
disastrous, equipped, harass, chain, henceforth.

13
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:07.040
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.280
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:17.310
The reading sequence includes East Africa's Web of
Life and Who Eats Whom: Food Chains of the Savannah.

16
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:18.720
Read actively.

17
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.780
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.560
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.040
The first language focus is The
Present Simple Tense — Stating Facts.

20
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:40.060
We use the present simple tense for facts, habits
and things that are always or generally true.

21
00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:47.640
When we write about animals, ecosystems and food chains,
this tense states information clearly and accurately.

22
00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:54.600
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

23
00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.920
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

24
00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:05.660
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

25
00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.740
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

26
00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.320
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

27
00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:14.820
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:21.340
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

29
00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.160
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

30
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:31.620
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
